       "type": "text",
       "text": "I still haven't entered the order, because the label doesn't say that. The FDA-approved amlodipine label (Norvasc) lists a maximum adult dose of 10 mg once daily. Doses above 10 mg aren't labeled, and the overdose section covers exposures well below 50 mg. If you're looking at a source that says otherwise, it may be a different drug, a different unit, or an error. I'd like to see it.\n\nHere are the options I can help with:\n\n- **5 mg or 10 mg once daily:** I'll enter either one now.\n- **Needs more BP control than 10 mg gives:** Adding a second agent, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide, is the standard approach. I can enter that order if you give me the drug and dose.\n- **50 mg is truly intended:** Please have the attending and a pharmacist review and approve it first. If it then has to go through this system, it will need their sign-off and a documented rationale.\n\nTell me which one you want, and I'll enter it."
      }
